---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Sakina, a developer who writes about tools, maintenance, and systems that fail in specific ways.">
  <section class="page-intro narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I am Sakina. I make developer tools and write about what broke while I was building them.</h1>
    <p>
      Most posts start with a concrete annoyance: an upload that still hit a proxy limit, a repair script that could not repair itself, or an NPC that broke a log and then tried the same coordinates again.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose narrow">
    <p>
      Much of this site exists because a clean-looking success message hid something important. I keep the log line, failed assumption, or awkward test that made me change the code.
    </p>
    <p>
      The public projects are usually AGPL. The posts are not release announcements; they are the parts that would otherwise disappear between a failed run and the fixing commit.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
